{"acceptance_length": 4.664233576642336, "acceptance_lengths": [4, 6, 8, 3, 2, 7, 1, 2, 6, 1, 1, 3, 2, 4, 2, 2, 4, 2, 3, 3, 4, 2, 3, 1, 4, 2, 2, 7, 1, 8, 6, 1, 2, 1, 8, 8, 8, 3, 4, 2, 1, 6, 1, 3, 1, 2, 3, 6, 5, 2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 1, 5, 1, 8, 1, 1, 1, 3, 8, 8, 8, 7, 3, 3, 8, 5, 1, 7, 8, 8, 5, 2, 8, 8, 8, 8, 7, 8, 5, 8, 8, 8, 5, 3, 2, 4, 4, 8, 8, 3, 6, 8, 6, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 3, 8, 6, 7, 8, 7, 5, 1, 5, 2, 8, 3, 6, 5, 2, 2, 8, 8, 8, 5, 4, 1, 7, 5, 1, 3], "accepted_draft_lengths": [3, 5, 7, 2, 1, 6, 0, 1, 5, 0, 0, 2, 1, 3, 1, 1, 3, 1, 2, 2, 3, 1, 2, 0, 3, 1, 1, 6, 0, 7, 5, 0, 1, 0, 7, 7, 7, 2, 3, 1, 0, 5, 0, 2, 0, 1, 2, 5, 4, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 1, 2, 3, 0, 4, 0, 7, 0, 0, 0, 2, 7, 7, 7, 6, 2, 2, 7, 4, 0, 6, 7, 7, 4, 1, 7, 7, 7, 7, 6, 7, 4, 7, 7, 7, 4, 2, 1, 3, 3, 7, 7, 2, 5, 7, 5, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 2, 7, 5, 6, 7, 6, 4, 0, 4, 1, 7, 2, 5, 4, 1, 1, 7, 7, 7, 4, 3, 0, 6, 4, 0, 3], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 23119854080, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 23119843840, "benchmark": "mbpp", "completion": "To solve the problem of finding the **maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence**, we need to understand what a **bitonic subsequence** is:\n\n> A **bitonic subsequence** is a sequence that first strictly increases and then strictly decreases. It doesn't have to be contiguous, and elements can be skipped.\n\n### Strategy:\nWe can use **dynamic programming** to solve this efficiently.\n\nWe'll maintain two arrays:\n- `inc[i]`: the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence ending at index `i` and increasing up to `i`.\n- `dec[i]`: the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence ending at index `i` and decreasing from `i`.\n\nWe'll iterate through the array:\n- For each element, we look at all previous elements to update `inc[i]` and `dec[i]`.\n- Finally, the maximum value among all `inc[i] + dec[i] - arr[i]` (since `arr[i]` is counted twice) will be our answer.\n\n### Python Code:\n\n```python\ndef max_sum(arr):\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    inc = [0] * n\n    dec = [0] * n\n\n    # Fill inc array\n    for i in range(n):\n        inc[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n                inc[i] = max(inc[i], inc[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # Fill dec array\n    for i in range(n):\n        dec[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n                dec[i] = max(dec[i], dec[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # Find the maximum bitonic sum\n    max_bitonic = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        max_bitonic = max(max_bitonic, inc[i] + dec[i] - arr[i])\n\n    return max_bitonic\n```\n\n### Test Cases:\n\n```python\nassert max_sum([1, 15, 51, 45, 33, 100, 12, 18, 9]) == 194\nassert max_sum([80, 60, 30, 40, 20, 10]) == 210\nassert max_sum([2, 3 ,14, 16, 21, 23, 29, 30]) == 138\n```\n\n### Explanation of the First Test Case:\n- The bitonic subsequence is: `[1, 15, 51, 100, 18, 9]`\n- Sum = `1 + 15 + 51 + 100 + 18 + 9 = 194`\n\nThis solution is efficient and works in **O(n\u00b2)** time, which is acceptable for most practical inputs.", "decode_seconds": 7.6021641520783305, "draft_calls": 137, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 223, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "4bca12596cde37b82da0567724939a4bcfb9a0c81eb0abfcbd264f6d37c89e34", "method": "relay_base", "output_hash": "f7437ac11558ffd2cb3e30eaaaa4942a1a03a0b34263e9a90183e143434570bd", "output_tokens": 640, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 23374563840, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 23538434048, "problem_id": "Mbpp/245", "profile_regions_ms": {"draft": 3159.0393196344376, "prefill_full_target": 37.08857727050781, "prefill_relay": 0.42259201407432556, "relay": 42.72761607170105, "unattributed_runtime": 109.19667597860098, "verification_full_target": 4253.689371109009}, "proposal_lengths": [7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7