\n\n```python\ndef max_sum(arr):\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    inc = [0] * n\n    dec = [0] * n\n\n    # Fill inc array\n    for i in range(n):\n        inc[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n                inc[i] = max(inc[i], inc[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # Fill dec array\n    for i in range(n):\n        dec[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n                dec[i] = max(dec[i], dec[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # Find the maximum bitonic sum\n    max_bitonic = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        max_bitonic = max(max_bitonic, inc[i] + dec[i] - arr[i])\n\n    return max_bitonic\n```\n\n### Test Cases:\n\n```python\nassert max_sum([1, 15, 51, 45, 33, 100, 12, 18, 9]) == 194\nassert max_sum([80, 60, 30, 40, 20, 10]) == 210\nassert max_sum([2, 3 ,14, 16, 21, 23, 29, 30]) == 138\n```\n\n### Explanation of the First Test Case:\n- The bitonic subsequence is: `[1, 15, 51, 100, 18, 9]`\n- Sum = `1 + 15 + 51 + 100 + 18 + 9 = 194`\n\nThis solution is efficient and works in **O(n\u00b2)** time, which is acceptable for most practical inputs.", "decode_seconds": 8.365630009677261, "draft_calls": 151, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 223, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "084b732347ce15a1a07d8e9f92e0c14cbc909c748e036d5d5b7681251e24fd0e", "method": "relay_three1", "output_hash": "f7437ac11558ffd2cb3e30eaaaa4942a1a03a0b34263e9a90183e143434570bd", "output_tokens": 640, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 23373426176, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 23561502720, "problem_id": "Mbpp/245", "profile_regions_ms": {"draft": 3495.9594914913177, "prefill_full_target": 36.77171325683594, "prefill_relay": 0.2938239872455597, "relay": 34.14982408285141, "unattributed_runtime": 120.42215209826827, "verification_full_target": 4678.033004760742}, "proposal_lengths": [7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7