 tuple and returned.\n\n### Test Cases:\n```python\nassert extract_even((4, 5, (7, 6, (2, 4)), 6, 8)) == (4, (6, (2, 4)), 6, 8)\nassert extract_even((5, 6, (8, 7, (4, 8)), 7, 9)) == (6, (8, (4, 8)))\nassert extract_even((5, 6, (9, 8, (4, 6)), 8, 10)) == (6, (8, (4, 6)), 8, 10)\n```\n\nAll assertions will pass with this implementation.", "decode_seconds": 5.289414630271494, "draft_calls": 95, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 219, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "4bca12596cde37b82da0567724939a4bcfb9a0c81eb0abfcbd264f6d37c89e34", "method": "relay_base", "output_hash": "9ff79809c26c5cfb8c648137f26307a47c9f79e49a0434cc95891dc7bc27d2f5", "output_tokens": 425, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 23335894016, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 23565697024, "problem_id": "Mbpp/580", "profile_regions_ms": {"draft": 2209.973705649376, "prefill_full_target": 36.63593673706055, "prefill_relay": 0.411327987909317, "relay": 29.83913591504097, "unattributed_runtime": 76.40281347185373, "verification_full_target": 2936.151710510254}, "proposal_lengths": [7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7], "rank": 0, "reference_answer": {"entry_point": "extract_even", "tests": ["assert extract_even((4, 5, (7, 6, (2, 4)), 6, 8)) == (4, (6, (2, 4)), 6, 8)", "assert extract_even((5, 6, (8, 7, (4, 8)), 7, 9)) == (6, (8, (4, 8)))", "assert extract_even((5, 6, (9, 8, (4, 6)), 8, 10)) == (6, (8, (4, 6)), 8, 10)"]}, "repetition": 0, "request_seconds": 5.289414630271494, "reserved_memory_after_bytes": 23565697024, "reserved_memory_before_bytes": 23565697024, "target_calls": 95, "time_to_first_token_seconds": 0.0, "turn_index": 0, "verify_count": 95}
